  "privacyIntro": "Stiže is private by default. Here's exactly what it does with data, in plain language.",
  "privacyLocationTitle": "Your location",
  "privacyLocationBody": "When you ask to see nearby stops and vehicles, your device's location is sent to our API with that request to find what's around you. It is used only to answer that request and is never stored on our servers.",
  "privacyAnalyticsTitle": "Anonymous usage",
  "privacyAnalyticsBody": "The app may record anonymous usage events (for example, that a stop was opened) to understand which features are used. These carry no identifiers and no accounts, and cannot be traced back to you.",
  "privacyTrackersTitle": "No ads, no trackers",
  "privacyTrackersBody": "Stiže shows no ads and includes no third-party advertising or tracking SDKs.",
  "privacyFeedbackTitle": "Feedback you send",
  "privacyFeedbackBody": "If you send feedback, your message — and the optional contact you provide — are stored so we can read it and reply to you. Nothing else is collected with it.",
  "privacyServicesTitle": "Services the app loads from",
  "privacyServicesBody": "Like any website, the app loads some parts from other services, which see your IP address as part of the request: map tiles for the area you view come from MapTiler, fonts and parts of the app engine from Google (gstatic.com), and the app and its API are served by Cloudflare. None of them receive your location from us or any account details.",
  "privacyOpenSourceTitle": "Open source",
  "privacyOpenSourceBody": "Stiže's code is open source under the AGPL-3.0 license, so anyone can inspect exactly how it works.",
